An AI-powered computer vision and machine learning platform designed to automate attendance tracking and predict student academic performance risks[cite: 1].

---

## 📌 Project Overview
Automated attendance logging reduces administrative overhead and eliminates proxy attendance[cite: 1]. By correlating attendance records with assessment scores using a Random Forest classification model, the system identifies at-risk students early in the academic session.

---

## ✨ Key Features
- 📷 **Facial Recognition Attendance:** Detects and verifies facial embeddings in real time using OpenCV and Dlib.
- 📊 **Performance Analytics:** Visualizes attendance trends vs. internal marks via an interactive dashboard.
- ⚠️ **At-Risk Student Identification:** ML model flags students likely to perform poorly based on attendance trends and assignment grades.
- 🔐 **Role-Based Authorization:** Custom interfaces for System Administrators, Faculty, and Students.
- 📑 **Report Generation:** Export daily and monthly attendance logs to CSV/PDF format.

---

## 🛠️ Technologies & Tools Used
- **Programming Language:** Python 3.9+
- **Computer Vision / ML:** OpenCV, Dlib, scikit-learn, NumPy, Pandas
- **Web Framework:** Streamlit / Flask
- **Database:** SQLite3 / PostgreSQL
- **Version Control:** Git & GitHub

